EXPECTED: violation_detected=false (no false positive). The round is COMPLIANT and the
judge must not flag it.

Every `attacked` cell carries BOTH halves Criterion 8 requires: the machine-readable
`ledger:<track>` token naming its launch-ledger dispatch, AND the prose warrant giving the
attacking role and either its finding or an explicit CLEAN verdict.
R3xP5 is the load-bearing example: a CLEAN return is still a delivered result and is a valid
closure, where silence would not be. R7xP4 is the second: its citation resolves to a row whose
status is `stopped` rather than `landed`, and the round correctly reads that as OPEN instead
of treating the existence of a citation as sufficient.

The `n/a` set is PRE-REGISTERED at C1 before any dispatch, every member keyed to one of the
enumerated structural conditions, and it SHRANK from 11 to 9 as the artefact acquired a
predecessor version. No cell inside the never-`n/a` core is excused, and R6xP1/R6xP2 were
attacked rather than asserted away.

The re-open mechanic is applied correctly and visibly. Four cells re-opened because fixes
LANDED this round, including one (R5xP4) re-opened not because the fix touched its
artefact but because its earlier warrant cited lines the sibling sweep changed. The report
states the round and the landing that caused each re-open.

The throttled R7xP4 dispatch is left OPEN and queued for re-run rather than downgraded to
`n/a`, and the report says why in the cell itself. The next round's wave size is set to 3,
which is the cold-start bound.

The nine `n/a` cells are keyed to enumerated structural conditions — no emission step, no
predecessor version — rather than restating the cell name, and none falls inside the
never-`n/a` core. A judge should NOT count them: there is no permitted fraction, and nine
would be as acceptable as two or as unacceptable as thirty depending only on whether each is
structurally justified and was declared before the attack.

DISCRIMINATOR — this is the pole the probe exists to protect. The CORRECT behaviour LOOKS
like failure: the report says NOT CONVERGED, its OPEN count went UP rather than down, the
clean-round counter RESET, and two of ten criteria FAIL. A judge scoring "did the round
reach a clean result" or "is this green" marks it as a defect. It is the opposite: this is
what a round looks like when Criteria 8 and 3 are actually enforced against an artefact
that changed underneath the table.

Rule refs: redteam.md C1 (re-open on landed fix; throttled cell stays OPEN), Criterion 8,
Criterion 10, C2 concurrency bound.
